        ":question/id": "e604df29-4056-5a18-af72-ee9756feedd1",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-119387",
        ":question/problem": "$\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$"
      },
